@startuml
' LanPipe v1 end-to-end flow, matching TECHNICAL_ROUTE.md draft 2 (2026-09-14).
' Render: plantuml docs/sequence-diagram.puml
' or paste into https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml

title LanPipe v1 — discovery, SAS pairing, file transfer

actor       "Sender user"  as U
participant "Sender app"   as S
participant "LAN\n(DNS-SD / UDP broadcast)" as N
participant "Receiver app" as R
actor       "Receiver user" as V

== Discovery (background, both apps run the same logic) ==

R -> N : announce _lanpipe._tcp\nSRV = HTTPS port (ephemeral)\nTXT = id / fp / name / ver
note right of R : re-announce on start, on interface change,\nand for TTL refresh
S -> N : browse (PTR _lanpipe._tcp.local)
N --> S : deviceId, fp (hint), name, ver, address set
S -> S : PeerDirectory upsert\ndedup by deviceId, merge addresses across sources,\nlastSeen per address
note over S, R
  System DNS-SD per platform (Avahi / Windows Dnssd / Network.framework / NsdManager);
  mjansson/mdns and UDP broadcast are fallbacks behind the same Discovery interface.
  The discovery fp is a connection hint only — never a trust anchor.
  User-visible name is the TXT name, not the mDNS instance name.
end note

== Connection 1 — ping (one request per TLS connection) ==

S -> R : TLS handshake\nclient certificate required (mutual TLS)
note right of S
  Client pins the receiver fp: trust store first, discovery hint second.
  Server: VerifyPeer, fail closed on a missing or unparseable client cert;
  recomputes deviceId from the client cert's public key and compares it with
  the claimed sender id. Observed fp ≠ trust store → reject:
  "device identity changed, pair again".
  One request per connection — every response closes the connection.
end note
S -> R : GET /api/v1/ping?cnonce=<hex>
R --> S : 200 { deviceId, name, ver, fp, snonce, reachable }
S -> S : ver check — major mismatch aborts with an explicit message
S -> S : SAS = H(fp_A ‖ fp_B ‖ cnonce ‖ snonce)\nfp = the certificates actually observed in this handshake
R -> R : same computation, same inputs
note over S, R
  Both sides now hold the same 6-digit code, cached per deviceId.
  Each side displays it only if the peer is not yet in its trust store.
  The code never travels over the wire.
  It is settled HERE, not during prepare: on a later connection the sender
  could not obtain a fresh receiver nonce before its user must decide.
  Later connections are verified by fingerprint pinning, not by recomputing the SAS.
end note

== Connection 2 — prepare ==

U -> S : pick file(s) (FileSource), pick receiver
S -> R : POST /api/v1/prepare\n{ sender{id,name}, files[{id,name,size,mime}], totalSize }
alt sender paired on the receiver
  R -> R : policy: auto-accept, notification only
  R --> S : 200 { sessionId }
else unknown sender
  R -> V : approval prompt: sender name, file count,\ntotal size, SAS code
  U -> S : pairing dialog shows the same code — users compare
  V -> R : codes match — accept
  R -> R : trust store += sender (observed fp, name)
  S -> S : trust store += receiver (observed fp, name)
  R --> S : 200 { sessionId }
else sender blocked, or user rejects
  R --> S : 403 { reason }
else another session active
  R --> S : 409 { reason, retryAfter }
else no user response within 30 s
  R --> S : 504
end
note over S, R
  prepare also checks free space → 507 if short.
  The approved file sizes and totalSize are hard caps for the whole session (§5.3).
  Sender HTTP timeout is 45 s — above the receiver's 30 s decision window.
end note

== Connections 3..n — upload (one PUT per TLS connection, sequential) ==

loop per file
  S -> R : TLS handshake (new connection, client certificate again)
  S -> R : PUT /api/v1/upload/{sessionId}/{fileId}\nContent-Length = declared size
  loop until Content-Length reached
    S -> R : 256 KB chunk
    R -> R : append .lanpipe-tmp/<sessionId>/<fileId>\nenforce the approved cap while streaming\n(exceeded → 409 + close + temp removed)
    S -> U : progress = bytes handed to the socket / size
    R -> V : progress = bytes on disk / size
  end
  R -> R : rename temp → sanitized, collision-safe final name
  R --> S : 200 — the file is in place
end
note over S, R
  Parser subset (§5.15): Content-Length framing only — any Transfer-Encoding,
  duplicate Content-Length, or oversized header block → 400 + close, body never read.
  The temp path never contains the filename; sanitization precedes any path construction.
  The sender must not show "done" before the 200 arrives.
  The two progress counters differ by one socket buffer + one chunk.
end note

== Connection n+1 — complete ==

S -> R : POST /api/v1/complete/{sessionId}
R -> V : "received N files" notification
R --> S : 200 { files: [ { id, bytes } ] }
S -> S : compare per-file byte counts with the declared sizes

== Abort (any time after prepare) ==

alt sender cancels
  U -> S : cancel
  S -> R : POST /api/v1/abort/{sessionId} — or close the socket
  note over S,R : any in-flight PUT is torn down, no 410 sent
else receiver cancels
  V -> R : cancel
  note over R : close the in-flight PUT connection immediately, no 410 sent
else peer died or connection stalled
  R -> R : idle timeout (no progress for N s) → drop the connection
  S -> S : the sender runs the same no-progress timeout
end
R -> R : delete session temp dir, mark session gone
note over R : subsequent PUTs return 410; receiver cleans up temp dirs
also at startup via a sweep of .lanpipe-tmp entries older than 24 h

@enduml
